      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"v\":1,\"title\":\"Video Reframe and Slow Motion\",\"subtitle\":\"Crop a vertical clip to a square, double its frames and save it at half speed. No models needed.\",\"author\":\"AusBoss\",\"layout\":\"card\",\"accent\":\"\",\"body\":\"## Start here\\nCopy `ausboss_pier_9x16.mp4` from the pack's `example_workflows/inputs/` folder into `ComfyUI/input/`, or pick your own clip on the Clip node, and queue. No models or extra node packs; the sample runs in seconds on a CPU.\\n\\n## What happens\\n1. **Video Crop + Rotate + Pad → Clip** loads the whole clip and crops every frame to a centered square: **Crop** mode with the **1:1** chip locked. Drag the crop box on the preview to reframe; rotation and padding work the same way.\\n2. **Math Expression** doubles the clip's fps (`a * 2`). **Frame Interpolate** resamples 24 → 48 fps with **blend**: every source frame is kept and one crossfaded in-between lands between each pair.\\n3. **Save Video** takes its fps from the Clip, not from Frame Interpolate, so the doubled frames play at the source 24 fps: **2× slow motion**. 97 frames become 194 and four seconds become eight.\\n4. **Select Frame** and **Compare** check the new frames: source frame 25 against result frame 50, the in-between halfway to source frame 26. Odd result frames (49, 51) are exact copies of source frames.\\n\\n## Try\\n- Same speed, smoother motion: wire Frame Interpolate's **fps** output into Save Video instead.\\n- Slower still: change the expression to `a * 4` and look at result frame 98 in the check.\\n- Blend softens fast motion. **Optical flow** gives sharper in-betweens but only uses RAFT weights that are already cached; it never downloads them.\",\"models\":[],\"packs\":[],\"links\":[{\"label\":\"Sample clip · ausboss_pier_9x16.mp4\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ausboss/ComfyUI-AusBoss/main/example_workflows/inputs/ausboss_pier_9x16.mp4\"}]}",
        ""
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note": "{\"v\":1,\"title\":\"Video Reframe and Slow Motion\",\"subtitle\":\"Crop a vertical clip to a square, double its frames and save it at half speed. No models needed.\",\"author\":\"AusBoss\",\"layout\":\"card\",\"accent\":\"\",\"body\":\"## Start here\\nCopy `ausboss_pier_9x16.mp4` from the pack's `example_workflows/inputs/` folder into `ComfyUI/input/`, or pick your own clip on the Clip node, and queue. No models or extra node packs; the sample runs in seconds on a CPU.\\n\\n## What happens\\n1. **Video Crop + Rotate + Pad → Clip** loads the whole clip and crops every frame to a centered square: **Crop** mode with the **1:1** chip locked. Drag the crop box on the preview to reframe; rotation and padding work the same way.\\n2. **Math Expression** doubles the clip's fps (`a * 2`). **Frame Interpolate** resamples 24 → 48 fps with **blend**: every source frame is kept and one crossfaded in-between lands between each pair.\\n3. **Save Video** takes its fps from the Clip, not from Frame Interpolate, so the doubled frames play at the source 24 fps: **2× slow motion**. 97 frames become 194 and four seconds become eight.\\n4. **Select Frame** and **Compare** check the new frames: source frame 25 against result frame 50, the in-between halfway to source frame 26. Odd result frames (49, 51) are exact copies of source frames.\\n\\n## Try\\n- Same speed, smoother motion: wire Frame Interpolate's **fps** output into Save Video instead.\\n- Slower still: change the expression to `a * 4` and look at result frame 98 in the check.\\n- Blend softens fast motion. **Optical flow** gives sharper in-betweens but only uses RAFT weights that are already cached; it never downloads them.\",\"models\":[],\"packs\":[],\"links\":[{\"label\":\"Sample clip · ausboss_pier_9x16.mp4\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ausboss/ComfyUI-AusBoss/main/example_workflows/inputs/ausboss_pier_9x16.mp4\"}]}",
        "ausboss_workflow_note_panel": ""
      },
      "color": "#14424d",
      "bgcolor": "#161f21"
    },
